  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">Up to the lookout</h2>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    The hike up was about four miles and 2,300 feet of climbing, just under two hours of moving time, crossing Sulphur Creek and Schriebers Meadow before climbing through old-growth forest into Morovitz Meadow. The junction with Railroad Grade, the alternate route toward Easton Glacier on Baker, was the part of the trail I'd never seen before, and it was stunning. There were a few creek crossings and a snow section that felt doable but sketchy. I should have brought microspikes, but did ok with poles.
  </p>

