  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    I made it to the lookout at 7pm. It was just me. Gorgeous, and quiet and I was giddy taking in the view. I ate snacks, journaled by hand on the porch, and just soaked in the view, watching the light change over the peaks. By 8:12 it was still light out and I was ready to turn in. I was stressed about the next day: I needed to hike down, drive back to Seattle, take a call, and then head to the airport to meet my family. I wrote it out on a note-card and felt like I had a plan, with some buffer, ready to go.
  </p>

  <img loading="lazy"
