  <h2 style="margin-top: 28px;">Sunrise, then down</h2>

  <p style="max-width: 75ch;">
    I was up before dawn the next morning for the sunrise. The teenagers had cell service somehow, so I FaceTimed my parents before I hiked out, then started down at 6am to make it back to the car by 8. Four miles downhill, including two of snow, then a two-hour drive, a noon call, a 1:30 call, and a flight that evening: it felt impossible to say in one sentence, but I felt like I had enough time to take it slow, and didn't need to rush. The snow on the way down was sketchy in a few spots, but I made it to the car right on time, at 8, and celebrated with a cold Diet Coke.
  </p>

